# Wave W17-Y (Vernal Path): petal post — a petal-drift marker post along the banks: a slim post with a drift of fallen petals gathered at its foot, pink over white, marking the lane the seasons use (design: unbroken flower banks either side of the hushed lane; the drift at the posts is the banks’ own shedding). On bloom turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 209’s pilgrim posts by the drift entire: those remember the dead, these mark a season passing.
